{"assets":["/statement-assets/af572790d886b5de9e6a69678560f5b9ffb802b8d91d49716b2f7199c5afce2c.png","/statement-assets/162f2e013870846392aa6a0cf5f28a7aef03de7ef88e81d97f016a79d39597dd.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"624","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Save Luke"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Luke Skywalker got locked up in a rubbish shredder between two presses. R2D2 is already working on his rescue, but Luke needs to stay alive as long as possible. For simplicity we will assume that everything happens on a straight line, the presses are initially at coordinates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"L"},{"kind":"text","text":", and they move towards each other with speed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v2"},{"kind":"text","text":", respectively. Luke has width "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"d"},{"kind":"text","text":" and is able to choose any position between the presses. Luke dies as soon as the distance between the presses is less than his width. Your task is to determine for how long Luke can stay alive."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains four integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"d"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"L"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v2"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ d, L, v1, v2 ≤ 10 000, d < L"},{"kind":"text","text":") — Luke's width, the initial position of the second press and the speed of the first and second presses, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single real value — the maximum period of time Luke can stay alive for. Your answer will be considered correct if its absolute or relative error does not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10 - 6"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Namely: let's assume that your answer is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the answer of the jury is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":". The checker program will consider your answer correct, if "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/af572790d886b5de9e6a69678560f5b9ffb802b8d91d49716b2f7199c5afce2c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 6 2 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1.00000000000000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 9 1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2.66666666666666650000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample Luke should stay exactly in the middle of the segment, that is at coordinates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[2;4]"},{"kind":"text","text":", as the presses move with the same speed."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample he needs to occupy the position "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/162f2e013870846392aa6a0cf5f28a7aef03de7ef88e81d97f016a79d39597dd.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". In this case both presses move to his edges at the same time."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"624A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/624/problem/A"}